{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Ideal.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Ideal.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"ideal ideal","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Ideal.md","fileName":"Ideal.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Ideal","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-13 19:40\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Ring and Ideal Foundations]] · [[Quotient Rings and Ideals]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Ring and Ideal Foundations","Quotient Rings and Ideals","Commutative Ring","Ring Homomorphism","Quotient Ring","commutativealgebra.pdf","essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Ideal.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Ideal.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"ideal ideal","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Ideal.md","fileName":"Ideal.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Ideal","heading":"Ideal","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"An ideal I in a [[Commutative Ring]] is closed under subtraction and under multiplication by arbitrary ring elements. The ideal generated by a collection consists of all finite ring-linear combinations of its generators.\n\nIdeals are precisely the kernels available to [[Ring Homomorphism]]s and the substructures by which [[Quotient Ring]]s are formed. Prime, maximal, radical, primary, and finitely generated ideals capture different structural properties.\n\nThe source motivates ideals by asking when multiplication of additive cosets is well defined. Closure under multiplication by every ring element is exactly the condition that makes the coset product independent of representatives.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Ring and Ideal Foundations","Quotient Rings and Ideals","Commutative Ring","Ring Homomorphism","Quotient Ring","commutativealgebra.pdf","essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pag